56
00:02:36,539 --> 00:02:39,230
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

57
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,299
Step 1.

58
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:43,740
Review personnel and unit
location-age settings.

59
00:02:44,119 --> 00:02:44,900
Step 2.

60
00:02:45,230 --> 00:02:48,040
Add stations and hospitals
as points of interest.

61
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,160
Step 3.

62
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:54,160
Add a relevant map layer, planned route,
or weather zone and review its audience.

63
00:02:54,359 --> 00:02:55,869
Now verify the result.

64
00:02:56,280 --> 00:03:00,879
Check marker age and source, POI
placement, reference-layer alignment,

65
00:03:01,059 --> 00:03:03,299
and the intended weather-alert coverage.

66
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:08,349
A common problem to watch for: Location
sharing requires client permission.

67
00:03:08,889 --> 00:03:12,869
Uploaded floor plans are reference
material; verify currency and

68
00:03:12,869 --> 00:03:14,789
alignment before relying on them.

69
00:03:14,999 --> 00:03:16,619
Your practice task is simple.

70
00:03:17,130 --> 00:03:21,309
Follow a sample unit and compare a
recent position with a stale position.

71
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:25,109
Record missing POIs and
outdated reference layers.

72
00:03:25,529 --> 00:03:29,329
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

73
00:03:29,779 --> 00:03:33,220
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
